WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:16,200
I just came across the sales pitch for store based probiotics. Their claim was

00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:23,480
that regular probiotics are 99% destroyed by your stomach acid and never reach

00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:29,680
your smaller testant to do anything for you. But the compounds that are

00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:36,080
spore based do survive stomach acid and go on to do their work. Have you ever

00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:43,480
heard of this? Is this a real thing? So there are benefits to store based

00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:50,760
probiotics for several reasons. It does survive stomach acid better. That

00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:58,280
figure that 99% of other probiotics are destroyed in the stomach acid is

00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:08,600
correct. So that is wrong sales pitch claim right there. I don't think you need

00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:14,800
everybody needs spore based probiotics. Matter of fact, good companies that are

00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:23,660
selling probiotics that have spore based and nuns, spore based probiotics

00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:28,900
typically recommend because the research recommends that you don't need to

00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:35,220
be on spore based probiotics indefinitely. So if you're taking a probiotic daily,

00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:43,820
you might want to take spore base. This is why my whole idea is to alternate your

00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:50,820
probiotics so that you're changing even companies that you're getting them from

00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:58,340
so that you're getting different varieties, grown different in different batches

00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:04,740
and it can have benefits that way. So I think spore based probiotics are great.

00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:10,700
We use ortho molecular spore based probiotics. We use mega spore, spore based

00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:17,140
probiotics. They are more stable. They are more expensive though. You don't need to

00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:23,380
take spore based probiotics on a regular basis. Maybe go through a model spore based probiotics,

00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:30,060
then switch to a different non spore based probiotic, then switch to a different probiotic.

00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:36,580
That's why we have multiple different probiotics on our store and I have said over and over

00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:40,540
together. I think there's benefit to rotating your probiotics.

